{
  "input": {
    "rationale": "The audit I recorded says four counts match their target's set and one does not, and the match that carries most of its weight is the commitment, whose map is built from voter entries and whose match function drops acknowledgements from anybody else. The first half of that was anchored, the second half - the drop itself - was not, and a reader checking the audit's central claim would land exactly there. I am adding that anchor to the saved behaviour on its existing id, with the map-level and call-level sites both cited, so the claim is supported at both ends rather than at one. This is an anchoring change: the statement, its conditions and its scope are the same, only the evidence behind one clause is now complete, so the changed premise records that the difference is representational. Nothing else is touched and no execution is spent; the run is at its budget and this is the last thing worth making right.",
    "sources": [
      {
        "id": "commitmentmatch",
        "file": "commitment.go",
        "start_line": 77,
        "end_line": 84,
        "kind": "code_observation"
      }
    ],
    "investigations": [],
    "knowledge": [
      {
        "id": "4d2efef6faed4deabf9c7d063d367373-knowledge-0",
        "ref": null,
        "kind": "behavior",
        "statement": "Auditing every quorum-like count in this package against the set its target is computed over leaves one mismatch and four matches. The mismatch is the leader verification, which credits the leader with a vote before consulting any configuration and counts acknowledgements from every entry of the replication state, non-voting members included, while its target counts voters only. The matches are: the election, which asks only voters for votes and tallies only those replies, with the quorum target computed over voters; the pre-vote, which likewise asks voters only; the commitment calculation, whose match map is built from voter entries alone and whose match function updates a server's index only when that server is already a key in the map, so acknowledgements from other members are dropped rather than counted; and the leader lease, which records a contact only for servers whose suffrage is voter. Commit, election, pre-vote and lease therefore all compare a voter-derived count against a voter-derived target.",
        "conditions": "This revision, the counts as written in the cited sites; the audit covers the quorum-like counts used for election, pre-vote, commitment and lease decisions, and does not cover message tallies that are not compared against a target.",
        "source_ids": [
          "electself",
          "commitmentworkset",
          "commitmentmatch",
          "quorumsize",
          "checklease",
          "verifyleader",
          "replnotifyall",
          "replstart"
        ],
        "executions": {},
        "knowledge": [],
        "changed_premise": "This revision changes nothing about what is claimed; it completes the evidence behind one clause. The commitment's exclusion of non-voter acknowledgements was stated from the map construction alone, and the call-level site that enforces it - the match function updating an index only for a server already in the map - is now cited with it, so the clause is supported at both the build and the call. The scope, the conditions and the other four counts are unchanged.",
        "affected_uses": []
      }
